# sem-data-visualizer — UX design sheet prompt
# Three display states of ONE container (buckets, query workspace, modal
# viewer) shown as three example pages on a dark minimal-tech canvas.
# Reference attachments are the judged renders from the private fixture
# build (see reports/tag-sem-data-visualizer.md); the tag's own harness
# captures are source-only until the bundle sync.

schema: "0.4"
id: sem-data-visualizer-ux-sheet
type: image
quality: high

prompt:
  text: |
    A precise UX design sheet for the SemText vocabulary element
    `sem-data-visualizer` — a container that wraps one or more named data
    buckets and renders each as a native table — shown as THREE example
    pages on a dark minimal-tech canvas (background #0f172a, card surface
    #1e293b, hairline borders #334155, blue accent #60a5fa, muted label
    #94a3b8, body text #e2e8f0).

    PAGE 1 — BUCKETS: the container holds TWO buckets and no query. A
    single right-aligned tools row sits above everything: a small pill
    button "Expand" and, beside it, a small pill button "Copy link".
    Below it, each bucket is its own bordered, rounded card holding a
    native HTML table: a bold left-aligned caption above the header row
    ("services", then "regions"), an all-small-caps muted header row, a
    faint sort glyph after each column name, hairline row separators, the
    last row's separator dropped. One bucket shows a pill button group
    under its tools row ("core" and "all") where "all" is filled with the
    blue accent and "core" is an outlined pill. Table content is plain
    monospace numerals and words, fully legible.

    PAGE 2 — QUERY WORKSPACE: one bucket table at the top, then the query
    block beneath it: an all-small-caps muted label on its own line, an
    editable monospace query field in a bordered rounded box reading
    "SELECT * FROM services ORDER BY port DESC", a small "Run" pill button
    with a muted "3 rows." status beside it, and the RESULTS table below —
    the same table chrome, with its own all-small-caps header row and a
    sort glyph per column, ordered by port descending (9090, 8443, 8080).

    PAGE 3 — MODAL VIEWER: the same container opened full-page over a
    dimmed backdrop: a large rounded panel centred in the viewport with a
    "Close" pill at its top-left, the expand/copy-link tools row inside,
    the bucket table live and readable beneath it, focus ring visible on
    the Close pill. The backdrop is a flat translucent scrim, never a
    blurred or coloured photograph.

    Typography: clean humanist sans for labels and pills, monospace for
    cell values and the query field, all-small-caps muted text for column
    headers and the query label. Flat, engineered, restrained — a
    documentation specimen of a data surface, not a dashboard
    illustration. Generous but tight vertical rhythm (.5rem between
    blocks), 12px radii, hairline borders throughout.

    CRITICAL: the authored payload (the markdown pipe table, the CSV
    lines, the YAML block an author typed into the document) is NEVER
    visible once a table is rendered. The rendered table replaces it.
  negative: |
    no raw authored payload text — no pipe-delimited markdown rows, CSV
    lines or YAML keys visible above, beside or beneath a rendered table;
    no duplicate table shown twice; no occluded or overlapping text; no
    solid colour block over words; no gradient glows; no decorative
    photos, icons or illustration; no chart or graph; no browser chrome,
    window furniture or device frame; no watermarks; no light-mode canvas;
    no red error text unless a value is genuinely an error.
  style: flat dark technical documentation specimen, minimal-tech design system

attachments:
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/sem-data-visualizer-fixture/sem-data-visualizer-multi-source-1280.png
    role: reference
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/sem-data-visualizer-fixture/sem-data-visualizer-query-1280.png
    role: reference
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/sem-data-visualizer-fixture/sem-data-visualizer-modal-1280.png
    role: reference
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/sem-data-visualizer-fixture/sem-data-visualizer-class-form-1280.png
    role: reference

output:
  formats:
    - format: png
      filename: sem-data-visualizer-ux-sheet.png
  dimensions:
    width: 1536
    height: 1024

requirements:
  modes:
    - name: buckets
      must_show:
        - one right-aligned tools row above the tables — "Expand" and "Copy link" pills
        - each bucket its own bordered rounded card with a bold caption above the header row
        - all-small-caps muted column headers with a faint sort glyph after each name
        - the view pill group under the tools row where the active view is a filled accent pill and the other an outlined pill
        - hairline row separators, the last row's separator dropped
      must_never:
        - never show the authored markdown/CSV/YAML payload as text anywhere on the card
        - never render the same bucket twice
        - never occlude a header or a cell value
    - name: query
      must_show:
        - the bucket table first, then the query block: all-small-caps label, monospace editable query field, "Run" pill, muted row-count status
        - a results table beneath with its own header row and sort glyphs, sorted by port descending
        - the query text legible and complete inside its field
      must_never:
        - never print the query statement as loose body text beside the chrome that already holds it
        - never drop the row-count status
        - never show the results unordered when the query states ORDER BY
    - name: modal
      must_show:
        - a centred rounded panel over a flat dimmed scrim, "Close" pill at its top-left with a visible focus ring
        - the tools row and the live bucket table readable inside the panel
        - the page content behind the scrim visibly dimmed, never replaced
      must_never:
        - never blur the backdrop or fill it with imagery
        - never let the panel exceed the viewport or clip its own content
        - never hide the Close control or drop the focus ring

eval:
  pass_threshold: 0.7
  criteria:
    mode_fidelity:
      weight: 0.3
      description: Each page reads as its state — two captioned bucket cards, a query workspace with chrome plus results, a modal panel over a scrim.
      fail_signals: [query page has no results table, modal page shows no scrim or no Close pill, buckets page shows a query field]
    payload_absence:
      weight: 0.3
      description: No authored payload text (markdown pipes, CSV lines, YAML keys) appears once a table is rendered; each bucket appears once.
      fail_signals: [pipe-delimited rows visible above a table, the same table rendered twice, CSV or YAML source lines next to a rendered table]
    chrome_legibility:
      weight: 0.2
      description: Captions, column headers, pills and cell values legible with AA contrast on the dark canvas; sort glyphs visible but faint; row-count status present.
      fail_signals: [muted text unreadable on the dark canvas, headers indistinguishable from cells, sort glyph missing]
    restraint:
      weight: 0.2
      description: Flat documentation specimen — hairline borders, 12px radii, no ornament, no chart art, no browser chrome.
      fail_signals: [gradient glows, decorative illustration, window furniture, a light-mode canvas]
  reject_if:
    - the authored markdown/CSV/YAML payload text is visible alongside a rendered table
    - any table cell or caption is unreadable or occluded
    - the modal page lacks a dimmed backdrop or a Close control
    - a light-mode canvas is generated
    - watermarks or browser chrome appear anywhere

tags: [semtext, vocabulary, data, table, query, modal, dark, specimen]